WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone is about to start!

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:08.580
Grandpa!

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.070
Grandpa?

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.360
He's Coach Endou's grandfather.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.360
Him?!

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.740
So you're Master D!

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.490
Master D, eh?

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:21.450
Is that how I'm called in the future?

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.140
You all have a good look in your eyes.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.020
All right!

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.100
I'll be the coach for this game!

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.800
You didn't come here to tell us about the strongest eleven in history?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.130
The strongest eleven?

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.030
Is that what's written in the holy book of champions?

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.350
I'll save that for later.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.840
For now, we've gotta win this match.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.450
The key to winning it is... 3D!

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.340
The key to winning is 3D, huh?

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:37.130
What does he mean by 3D?

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.890
The second half begins now with Raimon's kickoff!

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.590
3D...

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:47.770
Does he mean use the skies and not just the ground?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.190
Should you be thinking of something else during the game?

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:54.020
Tenma!

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.310
3D...

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.300
Maybe one of the "D"s is dribbling!

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.810
3D...

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.850
Something that pops out...

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:12.660
Avatars?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.990
Sword Saint Lancelot!

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.590
Armed!

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.090
Is he trying to fuse with his Avatar?

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.930
3D...

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.750
Maybe the "D" means defense?

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.030
Does that mean we need three defenders?

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.550
I'll stop you!

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:42.530
Leader!

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:44.720
The ball goes to Beta!

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:46.700
I'm scoring!

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.470
I won't let you!

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.500
Full Throttle Jump!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.180
Nishizono narrowly blocks the shoot!

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:03.470
Raimon goes back on the offense!

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.280
We have to find out what 3D means fast...

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:10.800
Leave that to me!

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.340
Go for it!

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:13.350
Daringly!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.350
Dynamically!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:15.830
Dive in and duel!!

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.690
They all start with "D," so it's 3D!

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.100
I missed!{カッコ悪っｗｗｗｗ}

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.480
I can get that!

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.090
Nishiki-senpai!

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.490
Bend down!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.610
Okay!

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.030
It didn't work...

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:39.000
You almost had it.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.270
Sorry to use you as a stepping ladder.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:44.010
It was only a second, but they had a delayed reaction.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.980
So I thought I could get it.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.750
Because the ball went in an unexpected direction?

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.430
Unexpected...

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:54.760
Three-dimensional... the key to winning...

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:55.700
That's it!

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.300
Everyone!

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.110
Connect the scattered dots!

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:03.280
Use all of the space there is above the field!

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.320
What's this?! A space opened up in Raimon's middle field!

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.720
Reiza runs towards it!

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.420
Their defense is weak.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.250
Are they luring me in?

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.290
Let's go!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:20.580
Okay!

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:35.060
Raimon is using the air fully and connecting their passes three-dimensionally!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.060
What?

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.190
Tenma!

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:39.700
Let's go!

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:40.500
Okay!

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:49.910
That's...!

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:53.660
A hissatsu tactics that will help them pass the ball without interference!

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:02.040
Demon God Pegasus Arc!

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.550
Armed!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.720
What?

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:14.990
Here I go!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.210
Cut the crap!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.230
What?!

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:28.650
Yes!

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:29.800
You did it!

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:31.090
That was an awesome plan!

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.490
As expected of the legendary Master D!

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:38.670
It was a hint to a new hissatsu tactics, was it?

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.010
Now, I don't know about that.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:43.860
Whatever it is you guys found...

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.290
...is the right answer.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:50.020
I knew right away once I saw the team.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.680
They were withering up in the face of a strong opponent.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.060
I could've said anything as advice.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.950
What they needed was the courage to plunge in and do what they do.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:02.120
That was all they were missing.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:07.040
Their tactics is troubling...

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:08.500
Over here!

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:09.900
Okay!

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.240
Oh...

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.950
Mixi-trans!{ﾐｷｼﾄﾗﾝｽ, trans as in transfer}

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:14.180
Tyranno!

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:25.210
Ancient Fangs!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.780
They tied with us.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:36.040
Is this a bad dream?

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:38.220
I didn't think they would be this good.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.060
The match resumes!

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.830
The ferocity of Protocol Omega 2.0's attacks increases!

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:51.600
In Raimon, Tenma's Avatar Armed and Fei's Mixi-trans are being guarded against so that the ball does not reach them!

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:53.760
Tsurugi!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.300
Sword Saint Lancelot!

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:00.720
Armed!

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.830
No good...

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:09.440
He almost had it...

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:12.150
Hey, pointy-head!

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:16.370
If there's nothing else you got, just eat your Avatar!

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.160
Eat my Avatar?

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.940
Only a few minutes remain!

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:28.010
It looks like whoever makes the next point will decide the match!

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.160
Sword Saint Lancelot!

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.150
<i>Eat your Avatar!</i>

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.440
I see...

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:42.580
I was trying to equip my Avatar on the outside.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:46.370
Instead of doing that, I should try fusing it inside myself!

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:49.590
Armed!

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.560
Yes!

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:02.360
You did it!

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:04.810
I'll stop you!

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:07.410
Keeper Command 03!

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.440
<Boom Shout>

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.940
This is bullshit!

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:20.110
All right!

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:22.230
Now it's certain we've won!

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.120
Let's hope so.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.870
Time is running out!

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:28.380
Hey, Einam.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.570
Yes?

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:31.880
Leave the rest to me.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:35.380
Ghost Mixi-max!

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.050
So we're going full power.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.510
Crush them!

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:43.390
Yes!

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.380
That's...

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:55.140
Beta's divided her power with the rest of them!

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.060
Leader!

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.410
Come out!

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:05.400
Goddess of the Vacant Skies, Athena!

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:08.290
Armed!

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:19.720
I'll stop you!

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:21.550
Don't get cocky!

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:24.170
Shoot Command 07!

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:25.360
<Double Shot>

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.420
Planet Guardian God Titani-

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:42.660
Hmph, there's no way you'd ever win against us.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.660
What was that power...

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.650
They're so strong now that they're in a whole different league!

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:55.710
Protocol Omega 2.0 suddenly powers up!

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.670
They've added more goals in mere seconds!

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.380
The match is over!

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:07.260
Protocol Omega 2.0 win with a turnaround score of 5-3!

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:09.670
This is their real power?

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.190
Now you realize how weak you are?

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:14.990
Master D.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:17.160
You need to disappear!

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:22.910
Lock-in Mode.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:26.960
That's...!

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:28.130
What?

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:32.540
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:37.820
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:45.160
I won't give in to this!

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:48.180
Grandpa!

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:49.680
Stop!

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:52.170
He's trying to bounce it back by willpower!

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:14.270
Daisuke-san turned into... a stone...

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.270
Now soccer is dead.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:28.120
What happened to him?

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.070
This is the Chrono Stone phenomenon.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:35.290
Most likely.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:37.580
Chrono Stone phenomenon?

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:40.820
Yes, a very rare occurrence.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:48.930
Endou Daisuke's resolve to not disappear clashed with the power trying to erase him.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:56.670
From the energy caused by that collision, Endou Daisuke's very existence became a point of contradiction in the timeline.

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:01.210
A contradiction in the timeline?

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:02.380
Yes.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:10.240
Because his existence no longer could be made consistent with time, he was compressed and made into a stone called the Chrono Stone.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:12.600
A person got turned into a stone?!

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:15.850
We have to change him back now!

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:18.790
Doctor Aruno?!

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.230
He always disappears right when we need him most.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.010
Honestly!

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:27.010
What an irresponsible doctor!

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:31.100
Hey! Treat your elders with respect!

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.020
Y-You can talk?

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.790
It's a weird feeling, though.

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:40.290
This must be a technique that is only made possible through Master D's willpower.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.540
But he can't stay like this forever...

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.360
First, we need to beat them.

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:48.090
Everything should go back to the way it was when that happens.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:53.960
Please tell us about the invincible eleven you wrote about in the holy book of champions.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:56.230
Sure, I can do that...

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:59.990
But this is just an ultimate dream of mine that I fantasized about for soccer.

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:04.840
It would be virtually impossible for you to gather its members.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:06.380
Do you still want to hear it anyway?

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.030
Yes!

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:10.450
I see.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.980
Then let me begin.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:14.190
First...

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:23.420
Power #1: A gamemaker of truth who can appraise people and the general situation, while combining both stillness and motion.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:31.290
Power #2: A charismatic defender who rouses up his team's courage, changing it into an iron-wall defense.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:40.300
Power #3: A midfielder of unparalleled accuracy, who can see into the future and attack the enemy's weak spots with his analytical reasoning.

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:49.150
Power #4: An iron-wall goalkeeper with the power to control a major country, along with the tenacity and will to carry out his actions.

00:14:49.710 --> 00:15:00.260
Power #5: A super tricky midfielder with a heart as big as the sea and who acts as the bridge between offense and defense.

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:08.330
Power #6: A speedy striker as quick as lightning, who cuts up the field like a lightning bolt.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:15.710
Power #7: A flying defender who controls the skies and makes the best use of his mastery with the air.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:24.180
Power #8: A dynamic midfielder who wields the power of ancient times and can split the ocean apart with his fangs.

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:31.610
Power #9: A fantastic libero with the ferocity of a beast and the wisdom of a sage.

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:40.520
Power #10: A king of midfielders who makes even the earth his friend with his absolute courage and unwavering ability to get things done.

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:48.900
Power #11: An all-rounder who pierces through all with the powers of the scorching hot wind and earth-shattering thunder.

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:55.560
Those are the conditions I have come up with for the strongest eleven in history.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:00.050
The contents itself are like a code.

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:02.770
I can't even imagine what sort of players they are.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:05.000
But we still have to try!

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:08.230
Let's find eleven players that fit those conditions!

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:11.570
But where should we start?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.500
Let me see...

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:17.910
If there was someone who fit the condition for Power #1...

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.120
Yes, Nobunaga!

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.910
Oda Nobunaga would be perfect.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.240
Oda Nobunaga?! From the Sengoku period?

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.420
He's not a soccer player!

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:33.610
No, if Nobunaga's abilities were put into soccer, he would make an invincible playmaker.

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:35.590
I see...

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:40.110
Nobunaga is the strongest military commander ever known, whose strategies were both bold and cunning.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:44.310
So we take Nobunaga out of the Sengoku era and make him play soccer?

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:48.150
See, I told you it was impossible.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.500
It's a dream that is impossible to implement.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.260
No way...

00:16:57.050 --> 00:16:58.300
We can do it.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.350
We can use the Mixi-max gun.

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:05.170
We'll go to the past to see him.

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.330
Then we'll take his power.

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:08.520
What?

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:10.840
Can you really do that?

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:11.600
Yes.

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:13.180
I see!

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:19.300
By going to the time period of that person and taking their abilities, we can make <i>ourselves</i>  the invincible eleven!

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:20.970
We can do it!

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:21.990
Things will work out!

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:23.530
Tenma!

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:25.670
You finally said it.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:29.890
This is interesting!

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:34.680
Let's travel through time to assemble the eleven players who can never be assembled!

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:38.340
I see. With you guys, it just might be possible!

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.010
So the strongest eleven in history will be realized, eh!

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:42.660
I'm getting excited!

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:44.360
Okay, let's do it!

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:55.120
I'll leave the strongest eleven in history to you.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:59.050
I will look and see if there's another way to save Endou.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:17:59.890
Yes, sir!

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:02.050
We'll bring them back no matter what.

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:04.760
Both Coach Endou and Daisuke-san.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.000
Yeah.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.730
First, we need to find an Artifact that connects us to Nobunaga.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.090
Oda Nobunaga.

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:14.470
Born in 1534 A.D.

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:17.640
He was born in the Owari Province now known today as Aichi Prefecture.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:21.230
At a young age, he was eccentric and called a fool.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:25.830
He instituted new tactics that used firearms, which were still rare at the time.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:30.430
He also had interests in various other cultures, even showing a large interest in tea ceremony.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:37.920
And after overthrowing the Muromachi shogunate, he was a great influence by the end of the Sengoku period...

00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:40.570
He was pretty amazing...

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:44.660
But there are no hints to what we can use as an Artifact.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:49.420
I know!

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.300
This, this!

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:55.850
Oda Nobunaga's samurai swords are on display in Inazuma Town!

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:03.070
So that long blade is the sword that Oda Nobunaga used... {katana refers to the longer sword, the short one is wakizashi. trying to signify one from the other}

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.440
This could be used as an Artifact!

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:06.290
Yeah!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.090
But we can't exactly take it...

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:26.180
You there!

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:28.780
Are you interested in swords?

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:33.460
You've been looking at that exhibit for hours.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:36.170
Well, um...

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:38.810
P-Please let us borrow this!

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:39.170
Tenma!

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:41.980
Please!

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:44.470
We absolutely need that sword!

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.150
We promise to bring it back!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.500
Why do you need it?

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:51.000
Well...

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:53.000
To bring soccer back!

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:55.700
Bring soccer back?

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.760
No, Tenma!

00:19:57.760 --> 00:20:01.330
If you say we're doing it for soccer in these times, she'll never let us borrow it!

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:08.510
You're Matsukaze-kun and Nishizono-kun from Raimon, right?

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:14.930
Truth is, I was once the captain of a pro all-women's soccer team.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:20.510
I watched your plays in the Nationals tournament.

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:23.560
Thank you for bringing so much excitement to soccer fans.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:28.700
But I just can't believe there's a soccer ban...

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.960
You're bringing back soccer, right?

00:20:34.220 --> 00:20:35.170
Yes!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.560
Very good then!

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:38.660
I'll lend it to you.

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:41.130
Really?!

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.270
Yes!

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:47.520
I don't know how this sword is going to help, but I trust you.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.590
Bring soccer back no matter what, you hear?

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:51.520
All right!

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:55.480
Artifact set.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:57.180
Wormhole cycle confirmed!

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:58.730
T minus 5 seconds to time jump!

00:20:59.040 --> 00:20:59.770
4...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.970
3...

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:02.090
2...

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:03.070
1...

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.280
Time jump!

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:14.080
We'll gather them up no matter what...

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:16.670
The strongest eleven in history!

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:21.700
We're here, team!

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:22.920
Here...

00:22:53.920 --> 00:22:55.950
We're in the Sengoku period!

00:22:55.950 --> 00:22:57.540
Time to find Oda Nobunaga!

00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:01.300
The Raimon Eleven heat up Sengoku!

00:23:01.300 --> 00:23:04.060
Next, We're Here! Nobunaga's Village!!

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:05.860
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:18.860
The Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone's proverb today is...

00:23:23.270 --> 00:23:26.600
The key to winning is 3D!

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:27.500
That's all!
